import{_ as o,o as a,c as t,ae as i}from"./chunks/framework.DQC_QtFV.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Models and Jev","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/guide/console/models.md","filePath":"en/guide/console/models.md","lastUpdated":1793164923000}'),s={name:"en/guide/console/models.md"};function n(r,e,h,d,l,c){return a(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[i('<h1 id="models-and-jev" tabindex="-1">Models and Jev <a class="header-anchor" href="#models-and-jev" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Models and Jev&quot;">​</a></h1><p>The agent is built on <a href="https://pi.dev" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">pi</a>, so <strong>every provider and model pi supports is available</strong>: log a provider in, or add a key, right here on the models page. The page holds three things: which model is the main one, Jev&#39;s key, and which provider search uses.</p><h2 id="主模型-the-main-model" tabindex="-1">主模型: the main model <a class="header-anchor" href="#主模型-the-main-model" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;主模型: the main model&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The model catalog comes from pi&#39;s agent directory (the built-ins, the pi.dev catalog, your own <code>models.json</code>) and is fetched at bot start and once a day after that, unless <code>PI_OFFLINE=1</code>; the 刷新目录 action in the page header fetches it again on demand. One chip shows the current main model and opens a searchable list. The main model <strong>must support vision</strong>: image understanding and sticker selection both rely on it. A model without vision stays listed and disabled with the reason. The 思考 select beside the chip picks the thinking level (off, minimal, low, medium, high, xhigh, max).</p><h2 id="jev-出口审查" tabindex="-1">Jev（出口审查） <a class="header-anchor" href="#jev-出口审查" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Jev（出口审查）&quot;">​</a></h2><p><a href="https://typesafe.ai/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Jev</a> is TypeSafe AI&#39;s decision model. It never writes replies; it answers yes/no questions with a probability: whether to join in, how long to wait before answering, whether to quote, which conversation goes first, whether a bubble may leave, whether a domain may be reached, which notes stay. Every outbound bubble passes it, so when it is unreachable the privacy check <strong>fails closed and not one message is sent</strong>.</p><p>This card shows its state (ok / missing / error) and the 设置 key / 更换 key button. The key is write-only, stored on the bot&#39;s side, and never returned to the browser.</p><p>The mode, threshold and extra criterion of each of its decisions live on their own pages: 回复时机 and 引用 on <a href="./conversations.html">Conversations</a>, 排队 on <a href="./advanced.html">Advanced</a>, 出口审查 on <a href="./safety.html">Safety</a>. A new decision ships in 只记录不生效 - the log shows what it would have done before it is trusted with anything.</p><h2 id="服务商-llm-login" tabindex="-1">服务商: LLM login <a class="header-anchor" href="#服务商-llm-login" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;服务商: LLM login&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Every provider pi registers, with the flows pi defines for it. Clicking one starts pi&#39;s own login; the browser only relays pi&#39;s prompts, stores nothing, can cancel mid-flow and can log out. Providers with no interactive flow are configured in the bot container&#39;s environment, as pi&#39;s own note says. Credentials are stored on the bot&#39;s side.</p><h2 id="搜索服务商-search-providers" tabindex="-1">搜索服务商: search providers <a class="header-anchor" href="#搜索服务商-search-providers" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;搜索服务商: search providers&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Web search and page reading go through here, keys write-only as well. Which provider is active is picked in the card, exactly like the main model; with only one logged in there is nothing to pick and the bot uses it (the page says 未选用 and why). DeepSeek shares its key with the model login above: logging in on either side logs in both, and logging out does the same.</p>',12)])])}const g=o(s,[["render",n]]);export{m as __pageData,g as default};
